{"content_hash": "540168098f8471df", "version_id": 893, "article_id": 90, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "John Lewis launches its 20th Christmas ad with a message about giving", "title_zh": "John Lewis 发布第 20 支圣诞广告，提醒大家别放弃用心送礼", "has_translation": true, "topic": "lifestyle", "source": "toodaylab", "source_url": "https://www.toodaylab.com/84280", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784210156339-43fceaca3548?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8am9obiUyMGxld2lzfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTQwMTMzNjd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Catarina Duarte on Unsplash", "author": "Catarina Duarte", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@cateduart?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/the-van-gogh-museum-building-with-a-green-lawn-ynFz9p5YcBE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(299, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(337, 46%, 48%)", "label": "LIFESTYLE", "seed": "b52bc96122d4"}}, "published_date": "2026-11-07", "word_count": 221, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "John Lewis has released its 2026 Christmas advert, called Gloria and Pickles. It is the store's 20th Christmas TV advert, and it asks people not to give up on choosing gifts with care.", "lead_zh": "John Lewis 发布了 2026 年圣诞广告《Gloria and Pickles》。这是这家百货公司的第 20 支圣诞电视广告，它提醒人们不要放弃用心挑选礼物。", "preview": "The three-minute film follows a grandmother called Gloria, who is getting ready for her family at Christmas. She looks for toys from her own", "preview_zh": "这支三分钟的短片讲述一位叫 Gloria 的祖母在圣诞节前准备迎接家人。她想找一些自己小时候的玩具，包括一只叫 Pickles 的拖拉小狗，因为她想让孙辈开心。然而，孩子们对这些旧玩具并不感兴趣。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 876, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 77.05, "size_bytes": 463248, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 252, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b1_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 79.175, "size_bytes": 476064, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 252, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/90/en_b1_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b1_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 84.65, "size_bytes": 508896, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 252, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/90/en_b1_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b1_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 72.55, "size_bytes": 436320, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 252, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/90/en_b1_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/90/en_b1_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 77.575, "size_bytes": 466416, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 252, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/90/en_b1_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@a16dcaf/content/data/versions/893.json", "paragraphs": ["The three-minute film follows a grandmother called Gloria, who is getting ready for her family at Christmas. She looks for toys from her own childhood, including a pull-along dog named Pickles, because she wants to make her grandchildren happy. However, the children are not interested in these old toys.", "Gloria almost decides to give them money instead, but Pickles tells her not to give up. In the end, she builds a secret playroom, and the family share happy holiday memories there. All the things she uses to decorate the room come from John Lewis, and the advert ends with the line \"Don't give up on giving\".", "The advert was made by Saatchi & Saatchi and directed by Lucy Forbes. Actress Kristin Scott Thomas plays Gloria, and comedian Paul Whitehouse voices Pickles. The music is Sam Fender's cover of the Rolling Stones song \"You Can't Always Get What You Want\", which is also sold as a CD and a record at John Lewis.", "The toy Pickles, a Fisher-Price pull-along dog first sold in the 1960s, costs £12.99 and is one of the store's main Christmas products. John Lewis first made a Christmas TV advert in 2007, although the adverts only became famous after The Long Wait in 2011.", "Many people see the John Lewis advert as the start of the holiday season."], "paragraphs_zh": ["这支三分钟的短片讲述一位叫 Gloria 的祖母在圣诞节前准备迎接家人。她想找一些自己小时候的玩具，包括一只叫 Pickles 的拖拉小狗，因为她想让孙辈开心。然而，孩子们对这些旧玩具并不感兴趣。", "Gloria 差点决定直接给钱，但 Pickles 告诉她不要放弃。最后，她布置出一间秘密游戏室，一家人在那里留下了快乐的节日回忆。她布置房间用的东西都来自 John Lewis，广告结尾出现了“别放弃用心送礼”这句话。", "这支广告由 Saatchi & Saatchi 制作，露西·福布斯执导。演员克里斯汀·斯科特·托马斯饰演 Gloria，喜剧演员保罗·怀特豪斯为 Pickles 配音。背景音乐是 Sam Fender 翻唱滚石乐队的《You Can't Always Get What You Want》，这首歌也在 John Lewis 以 CD 和黑胶唱片形式出售。", "玩具 Pickles 是费雪公司上世纪 60 年代推出的拖拉小狗，售价 12.99 英镑，是这家店今年主推的圣诞产品之一。John Lewis 在 2007 年推出第一支圣诞电视广告，不过这些广告直到 2011 年的《漫长等待》之后才真正走红。", "很多人把 John Lewis 的广告看作节日季的开始。由于成本高昂，公司曾考虑不再拍广告，但至少目前还在继续。"], "body": "The three-minute film follows a grandmother called Gloria, who is getting ready for her family at Christmas. She looks for toys from her own childhood, including a pull-along dog named Pickles, because she wants to make her grandchildren happy. However, the children are not interested in these old toys.\n\nGloria almost decides to give them money instead, but Pickles tells her not to give up. In the end, she builds a secret playroom, and the family share happy holiday memories there. All the things she uses to decorate the room come from John Lewis, and the advert ends with the line \"Don't give up on giving\".\n\nThe advert was made by Saatchi & Saatchi and directed by Lucy Forbes. Actress Kristin Scott Thomas plays Gloria, and comedian Paul Whitehouse voices Pickles. The music is Sam Fender's cover of the Rolling Stones song \"You Can't Always Get What You Want\", which is also sold as a CD and a record at John Lewis.\n\nThe toy Pickles, a Fisher-Price pull-along dog first sold in the 1960s, costs £12.99 and is one of the store's main Christmas products. John Lewis first made a Christmas TV advert in 2007, although the adverts only became famous after The Long Wait in 2011.\n\nMany people see the John Lewis advert as the start of the holiday season.", "body_zh": "这支三分钟的短片讲述一位叫 Gloria 的祖母在圣诞节前准备迎接家人。她想找一些自己小时候的玩具，包括一只叫 Pickles 的拖拉小狗，因为她想让孙辈开心。然而，孩子们对这些旧玩具并不感兴趣。\n\nGloria 差点决定直接给钱，但 Pickles 告诉她不要放弃。最后，她布置出一间秘密游戏室，一家人在那里留下了快乐的节日回忆。她布置房间用的东西都来自 John Lewis，广告结尾出现了“别放弃用心送礼”这句话。\n\n这支广告由 Saatchi & Saatchi 制作，露西·福布斯执导。演员克里斯汀·斯科特·托马斯饰演 Gloria，喜剧演员保罗·怀特豪斯为 Pickles 配音。背景音乐是 Sam Fender 翻唱滚石乐队的《You Can't Always Get What You Want》，这首歌也在 John Lewis 以 CD 和黑胶唱片形式出售。\n\n玩具 Pickles 是费雪公司上世纪 60 年代推出的拖拉小狗，售价 12.99 英镑，是这家店今年主推的圣诞产品之一。John Lewis 在 2007 年推出第一支圣诞电视广告，不过这些广告直到 2011 年的《漫长等待》之后才真正走红。\n\n很多人把 John Lewis 的广告看作节日季的开始。由于成本高昂，公司曾考虑不再拍广告，但至少目前还在继续。", "text": "The three-minute film follows a grandmother called Gloria, who is getting ready for her family at Christmas. She looks for toys from her own childhood, including a pull-along dog named Pickles, because she wants to make her grandchildren happy. However, the children are not interested in these old toys. Gloria almost decides to give them money instead, but Pickles tells her not to give up. In the end, she builds a secret playroom, and the family share happy holiday memories there. All the things she uses to decorate the room come from John Lewis, and the advert ends with the line \"Don't give up on giving\". The advert was made by Saatchi & Saatchi and directed by Lucy Forbes. Actress Kristin Scott Thomas plays Gloria, and comedian Paul Whitehouse voices Pickles. The music is Sam Fender's cover of the Rolling Stones song \"You Can't Always Get What You Want\", which is also sold as a CD and a record at John Lewis. The toy Pickles, a Fisher-Price pull-along dog first sold in the 1960s, costs £12.99 and is one of the store's main Christmas products. John Lewis first made a Christmas TV advert in 2007, although the adverts only became famous after The Long Wait in 2011. Many people see the John Lewis advert as the start of the holiday season.", "vocab": [{"word": "advert", "pos": "noun", "zh": "广告", "note": "英式说法，美式常用 ad 或 commercial", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "pull-along", "pos": "adj", "zh": "拖拉式的", "note": "pull-along toy 指可以拉着走的玩具", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "grandchildren", "pos": "noun", "zh": "孙辈", "note": "grandchild 的复数", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "give up", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "放弃", "note": "后接名词或动名词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "secret", "pos": "adj", "zh": "秘密的", "note": "secret playroom 秘密游戏室", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "direct", "pos": "verb", "zh": "执导", "note": "directed by 由……执导", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "voice", "pos": "verb", "zh": "为……配音", "note": "voice a character 给角色配音", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "cover", "pos": "noun", "zh": "翻唱版本", "note": "a cover of a song 一首歌的翻唱", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "although", "pos": "conj", "zh": "虽然", "note": "引导让步从句，不能和 but 连用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "cost", "pos": "verb", "zh": "花费；成本为", "note": "过去式仍是 cost", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T01:02:45.259729", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.4, "sm": 275, "em": 400, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "three-minute", "s": 0.4, "e": 0.925, "sm": 400, "em": 925, "cs": 4, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "film", "s": 0.925, "e": 1.262, "sm": 925, "em": 1262, "cs": 17, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "follows", "s": 1.262, "e": 1.562, "sm": 1262, "em": 1562, "cs": 22, "ce": 29, "si": 0}, {"i": 4,